tags: device-links, nvlink

A fact of a device: the devices of the node that have a direct link to this device,
which does not go through the host (for example NVLink between two GPUs).

The value is the stable ids (the fact device-id, 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:39363aeedc67ec903b169ac2d0c5c11974a7eec39c49eb908032d806f331a46d) of the
linked devices, sorted by their bytes and separated by commas. Example: gpu-1,gpu-2.

An absent fact: the node attests no link. The node is bound: it attests the fact.

